==Restrictions==
Max # of Deployable Cats: 15

==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 2~4 seconds<sup>60f~120f</sup>.
*50 [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*8 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*8 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Cumulus Gallus]] spawns as the boss after 36.67 seconds<sup>1,100f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*1 [[Mr. Puffington]] spawns once 30 Cat Units have been defeated.
*1 [[Mr. Puffington]] spawns once 90 Cat Units have been defeated.
*1 [[Mr. Puffington]] spawns once 210 Cat Units have been defeated.

==Strategy==
The enemies here push really hard, strengthened Cumullus Gallus and Puffington will nuke any units in the front every few seconds, and the peons, specially Sir Rel, will rush through your frontline and lose you ground with ease.

Since you have some time before Cumulus Gallus spawns, it is thus recomended to rush close to the enemy base before he spawns in order to have as much space as possible to fight, you will hopefully also juggle him against the enemy base for some time, this can be archieved using [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]]. You should aim to get at least half of Cumulus Gallus' HP in this starting push to then chip him down using fast units such as [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]].

[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]] shines here by clearing off any peons in the way of your attackers, specially Sir Rel, who can destroy all your units and push very far with great ease, be careful though, as Slime Cat will trigger any Puffington close to the frontline.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]]: Fast enough to not fill up the small cat limit but still tanky enough to keep the peons at bay.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]]: He does great at stalling here since he can tank all the hard-pushing enemies. It is recommended to bring Research [[Cat Combo]]s with him for faster spawn rate.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|Rushers]] with low cost and good damage perform great here. Use them while rushing down Cumulus Gallus at the start to get the most value out of them.

